{
 "id": "tidewraith",
 "name": "Tidewraith",
 "role": "Splinterborn boss · Ring 2 Coral Drift · flyer · Void Pull, Splinter Volley, Telegraph AoE",
 "hitbox_blocks": [
  4.0,
  1.0,
  3.5
 ],
 "notes": [
  "Facing north (-Z). Origin at the ground under its centre; it hovers with its belly about 13 px (0.8 blocks) up. 1 grid square = 1 texture pixel = 1/16 block. Hitbox 4 x 1 x 3.5 blocks around the body and inner wings; wing tips, tail and tendrils reach past it.",
  "Built on the vanilla Phantom: same rig and flight animations (body, head, wing_base + wing_tip each side, tail_base + tail_tip), scaled up and reshaped into a manta ray. Mapping: wing_l/wing_r = Phantom wing_base, wing_l_outer/wing_r_outer = wing_tip, tail/tail_tip = tail_base/tail_tip.",
  "The wings are stepped and swept back so the outline reads as a manta's triangle, not a rectangle. Skin is covered in pixel scales; five pairs of gill slits sit on the underside behind the head.",
  "Rounding rules (so it doesn't read blocky): 1) no single big slab; build each mass as a core box plus smaller boxes on its sides and ends, so corners step in 1-2 px. 2) Steps of 1-2 px, never 4+. 3) Taper thickness toward every edge: the wings go 3.5 px thick at the body to 1 px at the tip. 4) Droop the wing tips 1-2 px per segment, and in Blockbench rotate wing_l_outer / wing_r_outer 8-12 degrees down so the wing curves. 5) Trim and plates are thin inlays (0.5 px), not raised slabs. 6) Shade the edge pixels of each face 1 step darker (bottom) or lighter (top) to fake a bevel.",
  "Eyes are side-set (one on each side of the head). Coral cephalic fins curl forward like manta horns; the splinter gem sits on top of the head between them.",
  "Bones (16): root > body > head > fin_l, fin_r, splinter; body > wing_l > wing_l_outer; body > wing_r > wing_r_outer; body > tail > tail_tip; body > tendril_1..4.",
  "Animations: spawn (rises up past the island edge), idle (slow Phantom wing undulation), fly (Phantom flap), glide (wings held out, tips curl), attack (tail whip), hurt, death (spirals down and breaks apart), ability_void_pull (wings spread wide, pulls toward the edge), ability_splinter_volley (gem flashes, shards fan out), ability_telegraph_aoe (curls up, then a bubble burst)."
 ],
